This code uses a HashMap to store the query parameters and their values. It then converts the list of values for each key into a single string separated by spaces, which is used as the result.

Note that this approach assumes that the input URL does not have any anchor (#) in the path that may be present in some URLs (e.g., "http://example.com/path?a=1#anchor"). If you need to handle such cases, you should remove the anchor from the query string before parsing it.
